  "details": "Changing Network Ownership is a multiple step process that isn't corrected easily without starting the process all over again if one player happens to desync. Should a Synced Variable be used instead while keeping the same Network Owner, things are a lot lighter to duplicate for correction if it is ever needed via the Post Serialization Event. As is I can use Ownership Requests with a near explicit deny to act as a Network Call Event with access to the Player sending the call. This still isn't the most ideal though since it includes more traffic than necessary and is obviously not the use case it was designed for. Would be great to have a proper Network Call Event that allows retrieving the Calling Player as a VRCPlayerApi argument. \n\nAn alternative SendCustomNetworkEvent that may have even a single argument would be preferable. An int could of course be used for PlayerIDs, which would be sufficient for this request, and enable much more capability in the long run.",
